WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.320
- Since this is a 1980s
movie about frat brothers,

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:03.700
there has to be a scene about dudes

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:05.381
getting it on with an animal.

00:00:05.381 --> 00:00:06.214
(sheep bleats)

00:00:06.214 --> 00:00:08.440
I don't know how we're going
to be able to release this

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.192
on YouTube, oh my God.

00:00:10.192 --> 00:00:12.775
(upbeat music)

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:15.150
Welcome back to Laws Broken,

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:17.100
the series where a real lawyer pulverizes

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.140
your pleasant movies from the 1980s

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.000
by showing you how illegal everything is

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.000
because everything is illegal.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.600
I'm sure most of you have probably watched

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.630
Revenge of the Nerds
at one time or another.

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:28.290
Well specifically you probably watched it

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:29.750
at three o'clock in the morning on TBS

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:30.910
since that's the only time slot

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:33.840
where eighties frat boy
comedies were allowed to air,

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.820
albeit in highly edited form,

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.650
and you might not remember all
of the laws that were broken

00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:40.870
in Revenge of the Nerds, but I assure you,

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:43.140
there were a lot of them
because the main fixation

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:46.600
of these type of movies
is of course, girls.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:49.373
- There's 6,127 Students at Adams,

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.406
58% of which are girls.

00:00:52.406 --> 00:00:53.239
- So?

00:00:53.239 --> 00:00:56.410
- So that's 7,107.32 boobs.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.530
- [Devin] And thankfully,
we've come a long time

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:00.240
since this movie was released.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:02.250
Yes, Revenge of the Nerds
is from another era,

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.120
before nerds were celebrated,

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.420
part of the zeitgeists
and they had their own

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.850
award-winning TV shows.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:10.100
- Sarcasm.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:10.933
- You think?

00:01:10.933 --> 00:01:13.080
- But in 1984, people
were not so sensitive

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.360
to the plight of the nerds.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:15.460
Hence, we got Revenge of the Nerds,

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:17.400
a movie about a group
of criminal degenerates

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.340
and their plea for tolerance.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:22.730
So the criming kicks off with
what may be an actual murder.

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:24.900
As Lewis and Gilbert, the lead nerds,

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.460
walk through their Adams
College for the first time,

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:29.910
they walked right by the
alpha beta fraternity.

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:31.810
This sets up what is
probably the most quoted line

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:33.017
from the movie.

00:01:33.017 --> 00:01:34.055
- Nerds!

00:01:34.055 --> 00:01:36.283
- Ogre! Ogre! Ogre!

00:01:36.283 --> 00:01:38.780
- Yes, Ogre takes one look at
the pair of computer junkies

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:42.080
and lets out a primal roar, as one does.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:43.940
This sets Lewis and Gilbert on edge,

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:46.530
as they realized that they are
subjects of intense derision.

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:47.890
What they don't seem to notice is

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:50.290
that Ogre is dangling a man from the roof

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:53.360
and that man then presumably
drops 30 or more feet

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:54.193
to the ground.

00:01:54.193 --> 00:01:55.026
Did he die?

00:01:55.026 --> 00:01:56.060
Did he just break his neck?

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:58.460
Did we just watch a murder take place

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:00.130
in the first five minutes of this movie?

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:01.890
Well, the movie takes
place at Adams College,

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:03.870
a fictional college
somewhere in the Midwest.

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:06.120
Since I've never picked
on Nebraska before,

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:07.380
let's pick on Nebraska.

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:09.250
I'm setting the movie
smack dab in the middle

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:11.570
of the corn husker state, and in Nebraska,

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:13.220
a person commits murder
in the first degree

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:14.570
if he or she kills another person,

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:17.320
one, purposely and with
deliberate and premeditated murder

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:20.390
or two, in the perpetration
or the attempt to perpetrate

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:21.970
any other first degree felony.

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:23.080
I'm going to go out on a limb and say

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.380
that there just aren't many
circumstances that justify

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:28.170
intentionally dangling
a person off of a roof.

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:30.130
First degree murder carries
a potential life sentence

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:32.660
if the person dies, but if
there's just an attempt,

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:33.790
then it's a class two felony,

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:36.130
which carries a penalty of
up to 50 years in prison.

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:38.160
I think Ogre is probably
going to get out in 25

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:39.360
with good behavior.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.510
Now the plot, so to
speak, really takes off

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:43.180
when the alphas accidentally burn down

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:44.300
their fraternity house.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.350
In their defense, who knew
that playing with a Zippo

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:49.960
and drinking 180 proof whiskey
could lead to an actual fire?

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:51.410
So is this arson?

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:52.830
Well, probably not.

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:54.400
A person only commits first degree arson

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.310
if they intentionally
set fire to a structure

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:57.950
or start a fire while in the process

00:02:57.950 --> 00:02:59.470
of committing another felony.

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:02.560
The firestarter here appears
to be a guy named Haystack.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.740
I guess that explains this
movie's choice to put him

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:05.690
in overalls.

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:08.310
But at any rate he didn't
intentionally set the fire.

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:10.560
Accident is generally a defense to arson,

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:12.750
but he might also be able
to plead diminished capacity

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:14.430
because of extreme intoxication.

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:16.330
Now, intoxication is another version

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:18.470
of a diminished capacity defense.

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:21.070
Involuntary intoxication
is when someone drugs you,

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:23.470
or you take something that
you didn't expect to react to,

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:26.220
but voluntary intoxication
is when you really do mean

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.530
to get drunk, and of course you succeed.

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:31.690
Now getting drunk on purpose
is not a defense on its own,

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:34.570
otherwise we'd all get
drunk and commit crimes

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:35.470
without consequence.

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:36.640
However, if you're so wasted

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:37.850
that you can't control your actions,

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:40.225
then it might mean the
prosecutors would have a hard time

00:03:40.225 --> 00:03:42.710
proving that you set
the fire intentionally.

00:03:42.710 --> 00:03:44.140
So based on these defenses,

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:46.930
it might be the Haystack
is safe from charges

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:48.430
of first degree arson.

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:49.680
But that doesn't mean that everyone

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:50.760
is completely off the hook.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:51.850
The guys tell the fire department

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:54.230
that the fire was caused
by some faulty wiring.

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:55.240
This is probably a misstep.

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:57.260
It's definitely a crime to lie

00:03:57.260 --> 00:03:58.840
to law enforcement authorities.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:00.790
Nebraska law calls these false reporting,

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:02.920
quote, a person commits an
offense of false reporting

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:05.130
if he or she, a, furnishes
material information

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:07.770
he or she knows to be
false to any peace officer

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:09.580
or other official with the intent

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:12.940
to instigate an investigation
of an alleged criminal matter

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:15.760
or to impede the investigation
of an actual criminal matter.

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:17.960
This is a class one misdemeanor.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:20.320
Now the alpha betas face
up to one year in jail

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:23.240
and/or a thousand dollar
fine for false reporting.

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:26.070
But shout out to a young John
Goodman as the football coach

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:27.970
who helps the guys get
alternative housing,

00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:29.550
and there is of course
a big game coming up

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:31.080
and he doesn't want them worrying about

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:32.180
where they're going to live.

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:34.510
The Dean acquiesces to this plan,

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:36.290
which then leads to the
next scenes where the alphas

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:37.750
are storming the freshmen dormitory

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:38.770
and throwing everyone out.

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:41.419
- So as of now that dorm is ours, right?

00:04:41.419 --> 00:04:42.252
- Yeah!

00:04:42.252 --> 00:04:43.732
- Any room you want, ready?

00:04:43.732 --> 00:04:45.340
- Ready!

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:46.970
- [Devin] These guys are
probably the same ones

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:49.590
that 35 years later
would storm the Capitol

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:51.440
and basically do the same thing.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:53.930
Ogre then throws a man out the window.

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:55.910
Now, just because the
Dean consented to the plan

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:58.130
doesn't mean that the way
that they moved into the dorms

00:04:58.130 --> 00:04:58.963
was legal.

00:04:58.963 --> 00:05:01.700
Throwing a guy out the window
is still assault and battery,

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:04.070
and more precisely it's defenestration.

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.760
Defenestration is one of my favorite words

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:06.730
in the English language.

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:09.080
It's the act of throwing
someone out a window.

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:11.650
Now in the past, defenestration
has ignited multiple wars,

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:14.200
including the Bohemian Revolt
against the Habsburg emperor

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:18.060
Ferdinand II, which started
the 30 years war back in 1618.

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:20.010
Now here in America
defenestration is usually

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:21.870
just considered aggravated battery.

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:24.330
Charles Barkley once famously heaved a man

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:26.720
through a glass window after
the man harassed several people

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:27.553
at a bar.

00:05:27.553 --> 00:05:29.180
Barkley said what he
did was inappropriate.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:30.510
I'm going to defend myself.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:32.280
Let there be no debate, if you bother me,

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:33.700
I'm going to whip your ass.

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:34.890
The guy threw ice in my face

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:36.870
and I slammed his ass into the window.

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:38.260
Let it never be said that Charles Barkley

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:39.830
doesn't have a way with words.

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:42.170
Now Barkley was charged
with aggravated battery,

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:43.480
but the case was dropped after the man

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:46.010
who got thrown through the
window declined to prosecute.

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:49.200
That happened after he signed
a settlement with Sir Charles.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:51.720
Now in Nebraska, the state
charges this as an assault crime

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:53.880
quote, a person commits
the offense of assault

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:56.740
in the first degree, if he or
she intentionally or knowingly

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:59.180
causes serious bodily
injury to another person.

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:01.270
First degree assault
is a class two felony.

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:03.050
Class two felonies carry
you possible punishment

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:04.430
of up to 50 years in prison,

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.150
but I think the outcome
here depends a lot on

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:08.610
whether the victim was seriously
hurt or just banged up.

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:10.524
Ogre probably got first degree assault.

00:06:10.524 --> 00:06:13.750
Yeah, let's say 10 years, but
let's focus now on the nerds.

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:15.960
The nerds are now homeless
and seeking a fraternity.

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:18.280
So Betty Childs, the
leader of the mean girls,

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:20.300
intervenes to send them
to the alpha betas,

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:22.100
where they will be humiliated.

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:24.400
- Well, tell us what
frat do you think is us?

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:26.650
- You guys are alpha betas all the way.

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:28.830
- [Devin] Since this is a 1980s
movie about frat brothers,

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:30.900
there has to be a scene
about dudes getting it on

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:31.780
with an animal.

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:33.520
Here is that scene.

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:34.920
- You guys seem pretty cool.

00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:36.913
Take these for later.

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:42.801
- Rubbers? What do we need rubbers for?

00:06:42.801 --> 00:06:43.740
(sheep bleats)

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:45.970
- Okay, that is more than
enough of that scene.

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:47.480
We don't actually see Gilbert and Lewis

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:48.680
fornicating with the sheep,

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:50.910
but if they did, that is
the crime of indecency

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:51.990
with an animal quote,

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:54.270
a person commits indecency with an animal

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:57.070
when such person subjects an
animal to sexual penetration

00:06:57.070 --> 00:07:00.060
as defined in section 28-318.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:02.440
Lewis and Gilbert, therefore
indecency with an animal

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.960
as a class three misdemeanor,

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:07.350
get up to three months in
jail and/or a $500 fine.

00:07:07.350 --> 00:07:09.630
Now in our next scene, it
features multiple instances

00:07:09.630 --> 00:07:11.800
of the cinema sin of racial stereotyping,

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:14.590
where a frat bro asked
Takashi if he knows karate,

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:17.660
and then he puts a jockstrap on his head.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:18.821
- You know karate?

00:07:18.821 --> 00:07:20.470
- No.
- Good.

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:23.100
- Now under Nebraska law in 1984,

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:24.830
this is simple assault at best.

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:26.840
Misdemeanor assault is
assault in the third degree

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:28.760
and consists of either
intentionally, knowingly,

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:31.530
or recklessly causing bodily
injury to another person

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:33.730
or threatening another
in a menacing manner.

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:35.170
Now Takashi isn't seriously hurt

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:36.700
so this isn't a felony case,

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:39.230
but 21st century bullies beware,

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:42.530
because in 1997, Nebraska
passed a hate crimes law

00:07:42.530 --> 00:07:43.820
that enhances criminal penalties

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:46.860
when a person commits an offense
because of someone's race,

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:49.950
color, religion, ancestry,
national origin, gender,

00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:52.370
sexual orientation, age, or disability.

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:54.450
If found guilty of a
hate crime under the law

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:55.830
it acts as a penalty enhancement.

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:57.740
This means that a person will be punished

00:07:57.740 --> 00:07:59.160
for the next level of offense.

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:00.780
So if you were to use a racial slur

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:02.860
or ask a guy if he knows
karate before choking him

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:04.020
with his own jock strap,

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:06.420
expect prosecutors to consider
a penalty enhancement.

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:07.620
So random frat guy,

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:09.950
the penalty in this case would
be up to six months in jail,

00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:11.630
a fine of up to $1,000, or both.

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:14.750
Luckily for this guy, cancel
culture hasn't arrived in 1984

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:17.540
so this guy can probably
just get off with probation.

00:08:17.540 --> 00:08:19.740
Now in the next scene,
Lewis inadvertently invents

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:22.000
apartments.com, Zillow, and Airbnb.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:24.440
- [Lewis] Okay I've programmed
him with all the rental units

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:25.273
in the area.

00:08:25.273 --> 00:08:26.880
- And the computer he
built looks totally like

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:28.070
it's related to the dogs.

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:28.903
You don't see it?

00:08:28.903 --> 00:08:30.820
Well, just wait until you
see it in action later on.

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:32.690
- Now, Lewis's Zillow mode
brings us to this scene

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:34.040
where Wormser, the 13 year old,

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:35.370
goes to one of the apartments

00:08:35.370 --> 00:08:37.430
and is hit on by an adult woman.

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:40.847
- Hi, I came about the room for rent.

00:08:40.847 --> 00:08:43.420
- That's right next to mine.

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:45.240
It'll be perfect for us.

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:46.780
- [Devin] Why yes, she did answer the door

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:50.750
wearing a negligee and she
immediately offers the boy sex,

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:54.200
things that would only
happen in a 1980s frat movie.

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:57.260
Now this is criminal child enticement.

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:58.720
Quote, no person by any means

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:01.140
and without privilege to
do so, shall solicit, coax,

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:04.510
entice, or lure or attempt to
solicit, coax, entice, or lure

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:07.890
any child under the age
of 14 years into any place

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:09.900
with the intent to seclude the child

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:12.620
from his or her parent,
guardian, or the legal custodian

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:13.630
or the general public,

00:09:13.630 --> 00:09:16.210
whether or not the person
knows the age of the child.

00:09:16.210 --> 00:09:17.410
The perspective landlady,

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:19.660
arguably tried to entice
Wormser into the house

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:20.790
in violation of law.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:23.230
She's guilty of a class 3A felony.

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:25.110
Class 3A felonies carry
a possible punishment

00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:26.240
of up to three years in prison,

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:28.700
and an 18 month post release supervision

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:30.540
and/or up to a $10,000 fine.

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:33.190
And is it also contributing
to the delinquency of a child?

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:37.250
Well, under section 28-709 of
the Nebraska criminal code,

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:39.670
any person who by any
act encourages, causes,

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:41.430
or contributes to the delinquency

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:43.760
or need for special supervision of a child

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:46.250
under 18 years of age,
so the child becomes,

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:48.640
or will tend to become a delinquent child

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:50.410
or a child in need of special supervision

00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:53.290
commits contributing to
the delinquency of a child.

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:55.300
Now there's a lot of gray
area about what it means

00:09:55.300 --> 00:09:58.140
for a child to quote,
tend to become delinquent.

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:00.740
Wormser isn't a child in
need of special supervision.

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:02.720
In fact, he's actually a genius,

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:03.930
but the statute doesn't require

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:05.510
that the child actually become delinquent

00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:07.710
or need special supervision,

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:09.730
but only that the defendant
encouraged the child

00:10:09.730 --> 00:10:12.060
to become delinquent or to
need special supervision

00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:13.200
so that the child will quote,

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:15.530
tend to become a delinquent child

00:10:15.530 --> 00:10:17.440
or a child in need of special supervision.

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:19.350
So let's say this landlady
is getting slapped

00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:21.900
with six months in jail for her

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:24.290
tendency to create a delinquent child.

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:25.830
And then of course, the
computer that he created

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:27.790
basically goes off and
becomes (indistinct)

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:29.750
even attacking a human being.

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:31.690
Now, when the newly-minted
Tri-Lambs plan a party,

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:33.100
they struggled to get dates,

00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:34.570
and this is where the movie takes a turn

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:38.360
from Revenge of the Nerds
into Revenge of the Incels.

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:40.550
Of course, Booger has
been searching for dates

00:10:40.550 --> 00:10:41.920
at the local high school.

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:44.220
- Have any of you guys
got dates besides Gilbert?

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:45.340
- I do.

00:10:45.340 --> 00:10:47.370
- Yeah, but that's with a guy.

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:48.790
- What about you Booger?

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:50.750
- I've been out combing
the high schools all day.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:52.360
- [Devin] And although
we don't see his conduct,

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:53.300
if we take him at his word,

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:55.070
he has potentially broken several laws.

00:10:55.070 --> 00:10:57.301
First is stalking, which
is defined as being

00:10:57.301 --> 00:10:59.930
willfully harassed, intentionally
terrified, threatened,

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:02.300
or intimidated by individuals
who intentionally follow,

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.170
detain, stalk, or harass them.

00:11:04.170 --> 00:11:06.590
Harassing behavior occurs when
someone engages in conduct

00:11:06.590 --> 00:11:09.370
that quote seriously terrifies,
threatens, or intimidates

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:12.150
the person and which serves
no legitimate purpose.

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:13.750
This is a class one misdemeanor,

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:15.540
unless the victim is under 16 years old

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:17.060
when it becomes a felony.

00:11:17.060 --> 00:11:20.060
So Booger is almost certainly
facing up to a year in jail

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:22.120
and/or a thousand dollar fine just for

00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:23.610
stalking these teen girls.

00:11:23.610 --> 00:11:25.490
Now, after the frat
boys and girls continued

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:27.830
to mock the nerds, the
nerds formulate a plan.

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:29.810
For revenge, the nerds
decided not to commit violence

00:11:29.810 --> 00:11:30.670
against the alphas

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:32.690
because that would only bring
them down to their level

00:11:32.690 --> 00:11:37.690
so instead they decide to commit
violence against the women.

00:11:37.870 --> 00:11:39.530
- I know what we're gonna do.

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:40.790
- [Devin] Or in this movie's parlance,

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:44.040
they decide to have a fun panty raid.

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:46.940
These are the protagonists
of this movie, remember.

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:48.731
So let me give you a
rundown of all the crimes

00:11:48.731 --> 00:11:50.530
in this particular scene.

00:11:50.530 --> 00:11:51.593
First there's burglary.

00:11:51.593 --> 00:11:53.820
A person commits burglary
if such person willfully,

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:56.920
maliciously, or forcibly breaks
and enters any real estate

00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:58.430
or any improvements erected thereon

00:11:58.430 --> 00:11:59.750
with the intent to commit any felony.

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:02.750
The men broke in with the intent
of chasing down naked women

00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:04.440
and planting video
cameras on the premises.

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:06.390
I think that probably
qualifies as having the intent

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:07.280
to commit a felony.

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:10.630
Now in Nebraska, burglary
can be charged as either

00:12:10.630 --> 00:12:12.120
a class two or class three felony,

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:13.500
depending on the
circumstances of the case.

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.080
Class two felony in Nebraska is punishable

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:16.610
by up to 50 years in prison,

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:18.070
while a class three felony is punishable

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:19.260
by up to four years in prison.

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:21.890
So let's pretty much just
throw the book at Lewis

00:12:21.890 --> 00:12:23.840
and give him 50 years in
prison for committing burglary

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:26.380
in order to commit a
whole bunch of sex crimes.

00:12:26.380 --> 00:12:28.660
Then of course there is the guilt

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:30.610
of first degree criminal trespass.

00:12:30.610 --> 00:12:32.560
A person commits first
degree criminal trespass

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:34.670
if he or she quote,
enters or secretly remains

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:36.730
in any building or occupied structure

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:39.580
or any separately secured
or occupied portion thereof,

00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:41.300
knowing that he or she is not licensed

00:12:41.300 --> 00:12:42.400
or privileged to do so.

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:44.210
This is a first degree misdemeanor

00:12:44.210 --> 00:12:45.600
that probably will not carry more than

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:47.200
three to six months in jail.

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:48.220
And then the here's Lewis,

00:12:48.220 --> 00:12:49.940
terrifyingly just hiding in the shower,

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:51.560
then jumping out, yelling panty raid,

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:53.910
and then chasing the
naked girls down the hall.

00:12:54.769 --> 00:12:55.602
- Panty raid!

00:12:55.602 --> 00:12:56.450
(woman screams)

00:12:56.450 --> 00:12:57.450
- [Devin] Today, this would have ended

00:12:57.450 --> 00:12:59.450
with Olivia Benson
taking the perp to jail,

00:12:59.450 --> 00:13:02.450
but in 1984, it was played for laughs.

00:13:02.450 --> 00:13:03.760
But Lewis may be guilty of

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:06.010
second or third degree
sexual assault, quote,

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:08.170
any person who subjects
another to sexual contact

00:13:08.170 --> 00:13:10.650
without consent of the victim
is guilty of sexual assault

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:12.150
in either the second or third degree.

00:13:12.150 --> 00:13:13.760
And what is sexual contact?

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:15.020
You probably didn't ask.

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:17.870
Well, that is defined as
the intentional touching

00:13:17.870 --> 00:13:19.896
of the victim's sexual or intimate parts

00:13:19.896 --> 00:13:21.940
or the intentional touching
of the victim's clothing

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:23.370
covering the immediate area

00:13:23.370 --> 00:13:25.580
of the victim's sexual or intimate parts.

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:27.040
Now, unfortunately for the victims here,

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:29.270
sexual assault is only
a class one misdemeanor

00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:32.150
if the perpetrator didn't
cause serious personal injury.

00:13:32.150 --> 00:13:33.930
Now did Lewis touch any of these women?

00:13:33.930 --> 00:13:36.540
We don't know, but clearly
he was attempting to do that.

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:38.560
Third degree sexual assault
is a class one misdemeanor,

00:13:38.560 --> 00:13:40.580
which carries a possible
penalty up to one year in jail

00:13:40.580 --> 00:13:42.040
and a fine of $1,000,

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:43.270
and while the girls screamed,

00:13:43.270 --> 00:13:46.260
the nerds congratulate
themselves on their crimes.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:48.790
The nerds then install video
cameras in the sorority house

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:51.720
and then do terrible
things with that tape.

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:53.790
This is behavior that nowadays
would have gotten them

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:55.500
labeled as sex offenders for life,

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:57.820
but it's definitely an
invasion of privacy.

00:13:57.820 --> 00:13:59.700
So what laws do they break in addition to

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:01.700
breaking and entering,
sexual assault, and trespass?

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:05.330
Well under Nebraska criminal
section 28-311, quote,

00:14:05.330 --> 00:14:06.760
it shall be unlawful for any person

00:14:06.760 --> 00:14:08.860
to knowingly intrude upon any other person

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:11.590
without his or her consent
in a place of solitude

00:14:11.590 --> 00:14:12.423
or seclusion.

00:14:12.423 --> 00:14:13.520
Now that's a misdemeanor,

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:15.100
but they also violated section two,

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:17.260
which states it shall be
unlawful for any person

00:14:17.260 --> 00:14:19.290
to knowingly and intentionally
photograph, film,

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:22.480
or otherwise record an image
or video of an intimate area

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:25.400
of another person without his
or her knowledge and consent.

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:27.010
This is a class four felony.

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:29.400
The maximum penalty is
two years imprisonment

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:31.330
and two months post release supervision,

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:33.230
and a $10,000 fine, or both.

00:14:33.230 --> 00:14:36.170
So all of them, including
the 13 year old Wormser,

00:14:36.170 --> 00:14:38.320
are looking at a two year prison sentence

00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:39.730
for unlawful intrusion,

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:41.990
and of course later they
violate section three

00:14:41.990 --> 00:14:44.660
of that criminal code by selling
photographs of naked women,

00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:46.400
quote, it shall be unlawful for any person

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:48.070
to knowingly and intentionally distribute

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:50.640
or otherwise make public an
image or video of another person

00:14:50.640 --> 00:14:53.520
recorded in violation of
section two of this section

00:14:53.520 --> 00:14:55.320
without that person's consent.

00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:57.820
This is a class 2A felony with a 20 year

00:14:57.820 --> 00:15:00.200
maximum prison sentence, and
when this movie was released,

00:15:00.200 --> 00:15:02.620
there was no sex offender
registry, but today,

00:15:02.620 --> 00:15:04.860
if the men were over 19 and any victim was

00:15:04.860 --> 00:15:07.360
under the age of 18, they'd
be required to register

00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:09.050
under the Sex Offender Registration Act.

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:10.610
And they also allow
the 13 year old Wormser

00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:11.640
to watch these videos,

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:14.710
which probably contributed to
the endangerment of a minor,

00:15:14.710 --> 00:15:16.930
and please know that the girls
were fighting off the nerds,

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:18.500
and this is mostly in self-defense.

00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:21.680
Under today's laws, under
most states these days,

00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:22.740
they probably would have been justified

00:15:22.740 --> 00:15:25.300
in just shooting these guys
dead for home invasion.

00:15:25.300 --> 00:15:27.930
And then finally capping off
the biggest crimes we have

00:15:27.930 --> 00:15:31.190
that time that Lewis (beep) Betty.

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:32.420
Yeah, you heard me.

00:15:32.420 --> 00:15:35.380
Lewis puts on a Darth Vader
mask, impersonates Stan,

00:15:35.380 --> 00:15:37.930
and has sex with Stan's girlfriend, Betty.

00:15:37.930 --> 00:15:40.230
Now sex through deception is (beep),

00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:41.910
but it's not always punishable as a crime

00:15:41.910 --> 00:15:44.627
depending on how the
jurisdiction defines consent.

00:15:44.627 --> 00:15:46.050
(beep) by fraud was first recognized in

00:15:46.050 --> 00:15:48.380
American criminal law in 1865 in Michigan,

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:50.030
in the People v. Croswell.

00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:51.760
There, the Michigan Supreme Court upheld

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:53.590
the defendant's conviction
for (beep) by fraud

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:56.060
and stated quote, the
outrage upon the woman

00:15:56.060 --> 00:15:58.640
is just as great in these
cases as if actual force

00:15:58.640 --> 00:15:59.473
had been employed.

00:15:59.473 --> 00:16:00.730
That's because the women didn't consent

00:16:00.730 --> 00:16:02.310
to sex with that particular man,

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:04.650
which is the same situation we have here.

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:05.930
And of course there
always going to be people

00:16:05.930 --> 00:16:08.370
defending the scene by
alleging that in 1984,

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:09.730
no one knew it was wrong,

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:12.410
but that's kind of like saying
that in the 18th century,

00:16:12.410 --> 00:16:14.940
no one knew that slavery was wrong.

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:16.410
Definitely people knew.

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:18.870
In fact it was a crime back
then, so it's hard to say

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:21.720
that everything was hunky-dory back then,

00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:23.820
and here to add insult to injury,

00:16:23.820 --> 00:16:25.710
Betty is actually happy with the deception

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:27.950
and leaves Stan for Lewis.

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:29.000
- That was wonderful.

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:32.800
He did things to me
you've never done before.

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:34.120
- [Devin] And critics at the time

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:35.920
didn't even seem to be bothered by this.

00:16:35.920 --> 00:16:36.980
Gene Siskell loved it.

00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:39.350
He called the characterization
of the two "sweet"

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:41.660
and although Roger Ebert
listed the panty raid scene

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:43.370
as one part of the movie
that could put the boys

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:45.130
in a bad light, he called the movie great

00:16:45.130 --> 00:16:47.200
because of the human element.

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:49.087
- There's a human element
underlying this film

00:16:49.087 --> 00:16:49.920
that makes it interesting.

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:51.870
The story of these, of these nerds.

00:16:51.870 --> 00:16:52.950
- I don't know how we're going to be able

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:55.613
to release this on YouTube, oh my God.

00:16:55.613 --> 00:16:58.400
(upbeat jingle)

00:16:58.400 --> 00:17:00.460
And here's a quick
rundown of the minor laws

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:01.320
broken in this movie.

00:17:01.320 --> 00:17:03.010
The football team assaults Gilbert.

00:17:03.010 --> 00:17:05.380
The coach participates, even
threatening to break his neck,

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:06.380
attempted assault.

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:08.270
Here the frat guys mooned the Tri-Lambs.

00:17:08.270 --> 00:17:09.440
This is public indecency.

00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:10.810
The person commits public indecency

00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:13.120
if such person exposes, quote
the genitals of the body

00:17:13.120 --> 00:17:15.670
done with the intent to
affront or alarm any person.

00:17:15.670 --> 00:17:16.720
It's a class two misdemeanor,

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:17.950
and that would get these guys up to

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:19.480
six months in jail and a fine.

00:17:19.480 --> 00:17:21.870
The frat bros and frat
girls steal a farm truck

00:17:21.870 --> 00:17:23.857
and then turn the pigs
loose on the nerds' house.

00:17:23.857 --> 00:17:25.590
That's simple theft and vandalism,

00:17:25.590 --> 00:17:27.150
punishable by up to a year in jail.

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:29.900
The jocks placed a burning
nerd sign in front of the lawn,

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:31.710
vandalism, three to six months in jail.

00:17:31.710 --> 00:17:34.570
The nerds drip some heat rub
oil on the Alpha's jockstraps.

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:35.860
Is that a crime?

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:36.693
You bet it is.

00:17:36.693 --> 00:17:37.526
That's assault.

00:17:37.526 --> 00:17:38.900
And let's talk about the prison sentences

00:17:38.900 --> 00:17:41.140
for the two worst
characters in this movie.

00:17:41.140 --> 00:17:43.570
It was written with only
one main bad guy Ogre,

00:17:43.570 --> 00:17:47.140
but Lewis is also just
as bad, if not worse.

00:17:47.140 --> 00:17:49.377
Ogre probably gets 25 years
in jail for attempted murder

00:17:49.377 --> 00:17:52.200
and 15 for defenestration,
that's 40 years in jail.

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:54.320
And the ultimate perp
of this movie, Lewis,

00:17:54.320 --> 00:17:56.330
will probably go to prison
for (beep) by deception.

00:17:56.330 --> 00:17:57.420
Let's say 20 years for that.

00:17:57.420 --> 00:18:00.090
He's also guilty of two
counts of unlawful intrusion

00:18:00.090 --> 00:18:02.390
for entering and helping with filming,

00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:03.520
which is four more years.

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:05.120
And to that 50 years for burglary,

00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:07.110
one year for assaulting
the girls in the hallway,

00:18:07.110 --> 00:18:08.570
his total sentence is probably

00:18:08.570 --> 00:18:11.070
somewhere around 60 to 75 years.

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:12.540
Now this video isn't over.

00:18:12.540 --> 00:18:13.373
As you can imagine,

00:18:13.373 --> 00:18:15.010
there were a lot more crimes
that the nerds committed,

00:18:15.010 --> 00:18:18.650
but it's too hot slash
disgusting to go on YouTube,

00:18:18.650 --> 00:18:21.040
but you can watch the extended
version over on Nebula.

00:18:21.040 --> 00:18:23.650
And I'm thrilled to announce
my first Nebula Original,

00:18:23.650 --> 00:18:24.810
Bad Law Words Good.

00:18:24.810 --> 00:18:26.360
It's a long form documentary

00:18:26.360 --> 00:18:28.310
where I explore all the most common legal

00:18:28.310 --> 00:18:30.660
and linguistic ideas
that people throw around

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:32.800
in everyday life incorrectly.

00:18:32.800 --> 00:18:35.450
So strap in because it's
going to get really pedantic.

00:18:35.450 --> 00:18:37.790
It's a hilarious romp through
legal misunderstandings,

00:18:37.790 --> 00:18:40.250
logical fallacies, and
law and order parodies,

00:18:40.250 --> 00:18:42.510
and it's only available on Nebula

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:44.550
because Nebula is a place
where we can experiment

00:18:44.550 --> 00:18:47.230
with content and do things that
we couldn't put on YouTube.

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:49.560
And we're thrilled to be
partnering with CuriosityStream

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:52.290
because they are the go-to
source for the best documentaries

00:18:52.290 --> 00:18:55.100
